# Bumelerze — local environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (same directory) and paste in the two values from
# your Supabase project dashboard (Project Settings -> API). `.env` is
# git-ignored (see .gitignore) — never commit real values.
#
# These are the ONLY two values the app needs to switch from local-only mode
# (felt reports queue on-device forever; no telemetry ping is sent) to fully
# wired (felt reports sync to Supabase; the anonymous telemetry ping fires).
# No other code change is required — see supabase/README.md "Wiring status".
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_`-prefixed variables are inlined into the JS bundle by Expo/
# Metro at build time (the standard Expo SDK 57 pattern — no app.config.ts
# change needed). They are visible in the built app bundle, which is exactly
# right for the anon key (it's meant to be public; every RLS policy in
# supabase/migrations/ is written assuming the anon key is not a secret).
# Never put a service_role key in an EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable.

# Project Settings -> API -> Project URL
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon / public
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional — Map tab (web) basemap quality upgrade. Leave unset and the map
# uses OpenFreeMap (free, no key, no signup) automatically; this is a pure
# quality bump, never required for the app to work. Get a free key at
# https://cloud.maptiler.com/account/keys/ and paste it below to switch the
# Map tab to MapTiler's `outdoor-v4` (light, real terrain-relief cartography)
# and `dataviz-v4-dark` (dark) styles — see
# `src/features/map/style-provider.ts` for the exact style ids and how they
# were verified. If the MapTiler style ever fails to load at runtime (bad
# key, quota), the app automatically falls back to OpenFreeMap — the map
# never goes blank either way.
EXPO_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY=
